        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0747" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg657"/>

                <head>No. 289.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cadwalader to Sir Edward
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State, Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1875-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 18, 1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 21st of April
                    last, relating to an arrangement proposed by the lords commissioners of the
                    admiralty, governing the interchange of visits by the officers of the naval
                    vessels belonging to the maritime powers, a copy of which was promptly submitted
                    for the consideration of the Secretary of the Navy, I have now the honor to
                    inform you that a letter dated the 17th instant has been received from the
                    Acting Secretary of the Navy, in which it is stated that the proposition has the
                    full concurrence of the Navy Department, and that it will be embodied in a new
                    edition of Regulations for the United States Navy, which is now in course of
                    preparation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN L. CADWALADER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
